    "help": {
      "openTitle": "How to use",
      "title": "How to Use",
      "videoTitle": "Video Tutorial",
      "videoLink": "Watch a quick walkthrough: How to Use the Looting Helper",
      "step1Title": "1. Set Your Crafting Goals",
      "step1Body": "Use the search bar to find and add items you want to craft regularly. This builds your master list of requirements.",
      "step2Title": "2. Identify Loot Priorities",
      "step2Body": "The app automatically generates a list of all base resources and materials you need to loot to achieve these crafting goals.",
      "step3Title": "3. Manage Your Stash",
      "step3Body": "Mark items as already covered in your stash when you have enough of them. This reduces the list to what you still actually need.",
      "step4Title": "4. Optimize Your Raids",
      "step4Body": "Use the list during or after a raid to quickly decide what to keep, salvage, leave behind, or sell.",
      "exampleTitle": "Example Workflow",
      "exampleBody": "If you want to craft a specific gadget, add it as a goal. The visualizer shows the full tree from the final item down to base materials like Circuit Boards or Chemicals. When you find a topside item during a raid, you can quickly check which materials it salvages into and decide whether it is worth the inventory space.",
      "noteLabel": "Note:",
      "noteBody": "This tool focuses specifically on items needed for crafting. Combine these requirements with whatever you still need for expeditions or projects.",
      "learningTitle": "Learning the Game",
      "learningBody": "A key benefit of this tool is learning the relationship between topside items and the materials they provide. As you use it, you develop a better feel for what is valuable and eventually you will know what to keep without needing the tool."
